## HD Hyundai Electric Co., Ltd. financial statements, 6 years: Operating income of KRW 72.7bn but a net loss of KRW 40.2bn in 2020

The consolidated financial statements in the 2020–2025 annual reports that HD Hyundai Electric Co., Ltd. (267260) filed with Korea's DART electronic disclosure system, laid out by year. Figures from the 2026 half-year report cover a different period and are shown separately. **Every figure below is taken as filed in the DART submissions; there is no interpretation or outlook.** Amounts are in Korean won (KRW; bn = billion, tn = trillion).

### 1. Income statement — operating income and net income had opposite signs in 2 years

| Fiscal year | Revenue | Revenue change | Operating income | Op. income change | Operating margin | Net income |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 1.81tn | — | 72.7bn | — | 4.0% | −40.2bn |
| 2021 | 1.81tn | −0.30% | 9.7bn | −86.61% | 0.5% | −33.7bn |
| 2022 | 2.10tn | +16.53% | 133.0bn | +1266.43% | 6.3% | 162.0bn |
| 2023 | 2.70tn | +28.43% | 315.2bn | +136.93% | 11.7% | 259.5bn |
| 2024 | 3.32tn | +22.92% | 669.0bn | +112.22% | 20.1% | 498.4bn |
| 2025 | 4.08tn | +22.79% | 995.3bn | +48.78% | 24.4% | 731.8bn |

Revenue was largest in 2025 at KRW 4.08tn and smallest in 2021 at KRW 1.81tn among the six years. It fell from the previous year once: 2021 (−0.30%).

Operating income was largest in 2025 at KRW 995.3bn and smallest in 2021 at KRW 9.7bn. The operating margin was highest in 2025 at 24.4%.

**Net income was largest in 2025 at KRW 731.8bn and smallest in 2020 at KRW −40.2bn.**

### 2. Financial position — equity became 2.99x

| Fiscal year | Total assets | Total equity | Debt ratio | Current ratio |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 2.27tn | 679.2bn | 234.6% | 115.6% |
| 2021 | 2.21tn | 646.2bn | 242.8% | 111.6% |
| 2022 | 2.44tn | 831.2bn | 193.0% | 109.7% |
| 2023 | 2.91tn | 1.06tn | 175.3% | 131.8% |
| 2024 | 3.80tn | 1.51tn | 151.8% | 138.1% |
| 2025 | 4.77tn | 2.03tn | 134.6% | 134.4% |

The debt ratio was highest in 2021 at 242.8% and lowest in 2025 at 134.6%.

Over the same period total assets went from KRW 2.27tn to KRW 4.77tn (2.10x), and **total equity went from KRW 679.2bn to KRW 2.03tn and became 2.99x.**

The current ratio was above 100% in all six years, ranging from 109.7% to 138.1%.

### 3. Cash flow — negative in 2 years

| Fiscal year | Operating cash flow | Net income | ROE |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 204.5bn | −40.2bn | −5.9% |
| 2021 | 109.8bn | −33.7bn | −5.2% |
| 2022 | −124.1bn | 162.0bn | 19.5% |
| 2023 | −22.4bn | 259.5bn | 24.6% |
| 2024 | 1.03tn | 498.4bn | 33.1% |
| 2025 | 959.6bn | 731.8bn | 36.0% |

Operating cash flow was negative in 2022 and 2023. It was largest in 2024 at KRW 1.03tn.

ROE was highest in 2025 at 36.0% and lowest in 2020 at −5.9%.

